This Splunk Enterprise query searches Sysmon Operational logs and extracts the process executable name (`Image`) and executed command (`CommandLine`) from the raw XML event data. It then filters the 
results to show only events involving `powershell.exe`, which is commonly monitored because attackers frequently abuse PowerShell for malicious activity. Finally, the query displays the event timestamp, process
path, and command line in a readable table to help analysts investigate suspicious PowerShell executions.



index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "Name=[\"']Image[\"']>(?<Image>[^<]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Name=[\"']CommandLine[\"']>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)"
| search Image="*powershell.exe"
| table _time Image CommandLine
